.TH NEMUE 1 "November 2025" "Nemue 0.1.0" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
nemue \- Advanced security testing framework
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B nemue
[\fIOPTIONS\fR]
.I COMMAND
[\fICOMMAND_OPTIONS\fR]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B Nemue
is a high-performance security testing framework built in Rust, featuring network scanning, web content discovery, and extensible scripting capabilities. It combines the speed and safety of Rust with modern async architecture to deliver enterprise-grade security testing.

.SS Key Features
.IP \(bu 2
Network scanning (TCP/UDP/ICMP, IPv4/IPv6)
.IP \(bu 2
Web content discovery and fuzzing
.IP \(bu 2
Lua scripting engine (NSE-compatible)
.IP \(bu 2
OS and service fingerprinting
.IP \(bu 2
Stealth and evasion techniques
.IP \(bu 2
Vulnerability detection framework
.IP \(bu 2
Distributed scanning support
.IP \(bu 2
REST API and continuous monitoring

.SH COMMANDS
.TP
.B scan
Perform network port scanning
.TP
.B fuzz
Web content discovery and fuzzing
.TP
.B api
Start REST API server
.TP
.B monitor
Continuous network monitoring
.TP
.B distributed
Distributed scanning coordinator
.TP
.B report
Generate security reports
.TP
.B script
Lua script management

.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.BR \-h ", " \-\-help
Display help information
.TP
.BR \-V ", " \-\-version
Display version information

.SH EXAMPLES
.TP
Basic network scan:
.B nemue scan
.I 192.168.1.1

.TP
Web directory fuzzing:
.B nemue fuzz
.I https://example.com
.B \-b
.I dirs1k

.TP
Aggressive scan with detection:
.B sudo nemue scan
.I target.com
.B \-A

.TP
Subdomain enumeration:
.B nemue fuzz
.I example.com
.B \-m
.I subdomain
.B \-b
.I subdomains

.SH FILES
.TP
.I ~/.nemue/config
User configuration file
.TP
.I /etc/nemue/nemue.conf
System-wide configuration
.TP
.I scripts/
Lua script directory

.SH EXIT STATUS
.TP
.B 0
Success
.TP
.B 1
General error
.TP
.B 2
Invalid arguments

.SH SEE ALSO
.BR nemue\-scan (1),
.BR nemue\-fuzz (1),
.BR nmap (1)

